Shift:

Day Shift

Description:

*** APPLY BY INVITATION ONLY***

Overview

The Washtenaw Housing Alliance (WHA) is seeking a full-time employee to serve as a Housing Navigator as part of the WHA’s landlord outreach and engagement team. The Housing Navigator will work under the direction of WHA’s Community Housing Locator to:
Provide landlord recruitment, outreach, and education services;
Manage a database/software platform for landlord engagement and housing search assistance;
Compile data and create reports to identify and highlight landlord outreach opportunities;
Assist clients through housing search and permanent housing lease-up processes; and,
Provide follow-up services to landlords and tenants to ensure successful housing retention.
The position works in partnership with the WHA’s Community Housing Locator to expand housing opportunities for housing program participants and works closely with WHA member agencies’ staff and Washtenaw County Continuum of Care partners, such as Housing Specialists and Case Managers, responsible for landlord relations in helping clients obtain permanent housing. The position will also work closely with WHA’s committees, including but not limited to the Landlord Advisory Group and Housing Coordinators Network, to manage landlord outreach and engagement activities. It is essential that this individual works well independently and as a member of a small team in a fast-paced environment.

PURPOSE

Housing navigation is an important aspect of every community’s homeless response system and has been hailed as a best practice model in homeless services. These services are increasingly important as WHA and our partners strive to reduce emergency shelter stays and successfully re-house households experiencing homelessness as quickly as possible in Washtenaw County, MI. WHA’s centralized landlord outreach and engagement team seeks to be a bridge between homeless or at-risk households who may have barriers to housing, homeless response system staff, and landlords or property owners with available units in the private landlord market.

Responsibilities

A. Guide housing program participants through complex housing search and lease-up processes, including:
Provide support with housing search;
Assist participants with filling out housing applications;
Help participants secure move-in assistance;
Accompany participants to lease signings; and,
Assist participants with obtaining essential household items once housed.
Provide renter education and/or trainings to housing program participants;
Assist with researching the rental market to identify prospective landlords for housing programs and generate leads for outreach and recruitment;
Recruit landlords whose tenant screening criteria will provide opportunities for applicants with criminal backgrounds, including those with felony convictions, as well as those with eviction histories or no rental histories;
Market permanent housing programs, including incentives, to prospective landlords and property managers;
Assist with updating and maintaining a specialized database/software system with landlord and unit information, including:
Review and update information in the system to ensure accuracy and timeliness of data
Assist with user management, approval of property managers, landlords, and property related information
Provide support and training for landlord users
Perform data entry for tracking of housing search assistance services
Input and track data as assigned to assist management oversight of the database
Work with the Washtenaw Housing Alliance’s Landlord Advisory Group and Housing Coordinators Network to support effective landlord engagement strategies and to update and maintain a housing inventory database;
Conduct educational workshops to support property owners and other community stakeholders on a variety of topics, including on a variety of programs benefits and opportunities to increase awareness of programs that provide affordable permanent and/or supportive housing; and,
Perform other duties as required by the position

Qualifications

A degree in social work, or similar human services-related field, and/or at least three (3) years broad-based work experience in housing, homeless services, property management, and/or community development;
Lived experience of homelessness, housing insecurity, and/or justice-involvement will be valued alongside professional credentials;
Prior experience working in settings with low-income individuals and families and people experiencing homelessness and housing insecurity;
Excellent verbal and written communication skills;
Experience with different technologies including Microsoft Office Suite; Google; Video conferencing; Email; and, Data management tools;
Experience with data entry accuracy and reporting;
Demonstrated capacity to exercise discretion and sound judgment in general matters and in handling confidential information;
Strong personal commitment to prevent and end homelessness;
Knowledge and adherence to “Housing First” principles and strategies for ending homelessness;
Ability to work independently, with initiative and resourcefulness; and,
Ability to work collaboratively with diverse partners and groups.

Our Commitment

Rooted in our Mission and Core Values, we honor the dignity of every person and recognize the unique perspectives, experiences, and talents each colleague brings. By finding common ground and embracing our differences, we grow stronger together and deliver more compassionate, person-centered care. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law.

